{% comment %}
  Shopify Snippet: Store currency price

  KSA store (sa.balqees.com): this snippet previously rendered the new
  UAE Dirham symbol. It now renders the shop's own currency format
  (Saudi Riyal / SAR) so prices are consistent across the storefront.

  Class names are intentionally unchanged (.dirham-price / .dirham-amount)
  so existing theme CSS keeps applying.

  Usage:
  {% render 'dirham-symbol-shopify', amount: product.price %}

  Parameters:
  - amount: The price amount in cents (required)
  - show_decimals: true/false (optional, default: true)
  - class: Additional CSS classes (optional)
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign show_decimals = show_decimals | default: true
  assign formatted_amount = amount | money

  if show_decimals == false
    assign formatted_amount = amount | money | remove: '.00'
  endif
%}

<span class="dirham-price {{ class }}">
  <span class="dirham-amount">{{ formatted_amount }}</span>
</span>
